578 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 269 0 R
/E (Singapore stays prime at 4.19 in 2007 to 4.30 in 2022, up +0.11 and consistently above 4.00, showing single-hub port and customs efficiency that creates 1.30 gap vs Indonesia at 3.00. Thailand holds steady from 3.31 to 3.50, up +0.19 driven by Laem Chabang port expansion and Eastern Economic Corridor, staying second among the four with stable growth despite political cycles.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
579 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 269 0 R
/E (01)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
580 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 269 0 R
/E (Vietnam surges from 2.89 to 3.30, up +0.41 the biggest leap among majors, driven by manufacturing shift from China and deep-water port investment that now ties Philippines at 3.30, overtaking Indonesia. Indonesia stuck from 3.01 to 3.00, down -0.01 the only major declining, from above Vietnam in 2007 at 3.01 vs 2.89 to 0.30 below Vietnam in 2022 at 3.00 vs 3.30. This is the Archipelago Paradox, 17,000 islands create 17,000 last-mile bottlenecks instead of economies of scale, with fragmented ports adding 2-3 days vs Singapore single hub.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
